<title>ARGENTINA: Astra buys control of two firms for $75 mln.</title>
<headline>Astra buys control of two firms for $75 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine oil firm Astra CAPSA, controlled by Spain's Repsol, said Monday it agreed to buy a controlling stake in two companies for a total of $75.4 million.</p>
<p>&quot;We agreed to buy a 95.4 percent stake of Algas SA and a 89 percent stake of Poligas Lujan SA for $75.4 million,&quot; Astra told the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
